From 6fbedda80c80279878b51f6dfb58b0dc45fa66d2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lakr <git@qaq.wiki>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 06:44:42 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] tests: run the no-dispatch section against real regions
 and an ARM walk

test-reims-vgpu-ram covers the RAM-only copy with a fake memory map.
This covers what it cannot: memory_no_dispatch_begin() and the
reims-vgpu callbacks against real MemoryRegions, a real ARM CPU's
page-table walk, and the real BQL.

The test is an emulator built from the same objects as
qemu-system-aarch64 with its own main(). It boots an idle virt machine
(-S, TCG), adds a counting MMIO region, a ROM, and a RAM region with a
second MMIO region right after it, and drives them from worker threads
while the main thread holds the BQL; a worker that tried to take the
BQL would hang, and the test fails if one does not finish. It checks:

- address_space_read/write and the ld/st helpers on MMIO inside a
  section fail with MEMTX_ACCESS_ERROR, and RAM still works;
- sections nest, and after the outermost ends an access dispatches
  again, with the BQL;
- another thread outside a section dispatches as usual;
- a walk whose level 0 or level 1 table is in the MMIO region fails
  inside a section without reading it, and reads it outside one; a walk
  through RAM completes inside one;
- read_gpa/write_gpa refuse MMIO, a range running from RAM into MMIO
  (with the RAM half left unwritten) and a write to ROM, and refuse a
  range that wraps or has no buffer;
- read_kva across a RAM page into a page that maps MMIO is refused with
  the caller's buffer untouched, and wrapping or missing buffers are -3.

In each case the MMIO region's callbacks ran zero times. The test is not
built by default; it is in the unit suite.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 1c68d09c7050d2c052da75403ca2147ddcdf0e92)
